BD2: What different ways do the papers turn examples or user intent into a program? Compare input-output example methods with at least one other kind of specification or interaction, explain how candidate programs are searched or ranked, and describe a practical ambiguity or feedback challenge.
Subqueries: ["program synthesis input-output examples candidate program search ranking ambiguity feedback user intent specification papers", "code generation natural language specification interactive feedback program synthesis ranking search methods papers", "program synthesis examples versus sketches types constraints tests user interaction ambiguity challenge candidate programs ranked"]
